<BaseLayout
  title="IgG vs IgM Antibody Test — Acute vs Past Infection | Progene Bio"
  description="IgG vs IgM antibody tests — IgM indicates recent infection, IgG indicates past or established immunity. How to interpret serology."
  canonical="/comparisons/igg-vs-igm/"
>

  <h1>IgG vs IgM Antibody Test</h1>

  <div class="card">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th></th><th>IgM</th><th>IgG</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Appears</th><td>First (days after infection)</td><td>Later (weeks)</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Indicates</th><td>Recent / acute infection</td><td>Past infection / established immunity</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Persistence</th><td>Weeks–months</td><td>Years / lifelong</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Interpretation</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>IgM+/IgG−</strong> = recent infection (acute phase)</li>
    <li><strong>IgM+/IgG+</strong> = active or late-acute infection</li>
    <li><strong>IgM−/IgG+</strong> = past infection or immunity</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Timing depends on the pathogen — see <a href="/comparisons/dengue-ns1-vs-igg-igm/">Dengue NS1 vs IgM/IgG</a> for a worked example.
  </p>

</BaseLayout>
